  Reading: a positive separation means the covariate was measured after the
  creatinine the row is anchored on, so that row's feature vector contains
  information not available at the anchor timestamp. Whether that matters depends
  on the claim being made: for a retrospective benchmark on a reconstructed
  snapshot it is a documented property of the reconstruction; for a prospective
  claim it is an information cutoff that would have to be defined and enforced.
  Quantifying it does not settle which claim the manuscript makes — see Gap 8.

